WEBVTT

00:02.550 --> 00:03.551
KATARA: Water.

00:04.928 --> 00:05.929
Earth.

00:06.846 --> 00:07.847
Fire.

00:08.890 --> 00:09.891
Air.

00:11.434 --> 00:15.396
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.522 --> 00:18.566
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.859 --> 00:22.487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.612 --> 00:23.821
could stop them.

00:23.947 --> 00:26.241
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.575 --> 00:29.702
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

00:29.827 --> 00:32.914
the new Avatar,
an Airbender named Aang.

00:33.039 --> 00:35.250
And although
his airbending skills are great,

00:35.375 --> 00:37.669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.794 --> 00:39.003
AANG: Oof!

00:39.128 --> 00:42.090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:42.215 --> 00:45.718
♪

00:56.169 --> 01:00.257
♪

01:02.384 --> 01:04.052
♪

01:05.178 --> 01:09.558
[ missiles exploding ]

01:10.308 --> 01:16.273
♪

01:17.232 --> 01:18.608
Dad!

01:19.860 --> 01:21.361
You're on your feet again.

01:21.486 --> 01:22.779
Thanks to your sister.

01:22.863 --> 01:24.406
I'm in no shape to fight,

01:24.573 --> 01:26.408
but maybe there is some way
I could help.

01:26.533 --> 01:27.701
Everything's going smoothly,

01:27.826 --> 01:29.703
and the eclipse hasn't even
kicked in yet.

01:29.828 --> 01:32.247
Let's hope
our luck holds out.

01:32.372 --> 01:34.291
Katara, you seem distracted.

01:34.583 --> 01:36.126
Is something wrong?

01:36.251 --> 01:37.252
Yeah.

01:37.377 --> 01:39.963
Is that―is that Aang?

01:40.088 --> 01:41.298
What?

01:41.423 --> 01:43.758
♪

01:43.884 --> 01:45.385
Please tell you're here
because the Fire Lord

01:45.510 --> 01:46.511
turned out to be a big wimp,

01:46.595 --> 01:48.722
and you didn't even need
the eclipse to take him down?

01:49.014 --> 01:50.307
He wasn't home.

01:50.557 --> 01:52.058
No one was.

01:52.142 --> 01:55.478
The entire palace city
is abandoned.

01:55.562 --> 01:56.730
They knew.

01:56.813 --> 01:58.023
AANG: It's over.

01:58.106 --> 02:00.191
The Fire Lord
is probably long gone.

02:00.317 --> 02:01.985
Far away on some remote island

02:02.110 --> 02:03.904
where he'll be safe
during the eclipse.

02:04.279 --> 02:05.572
No.

02:05.697 --> 02:07.574
My instincts tell me
he wouldn't go too far.

02:07.782 --> 02:09.159
He would have a secret bunker.

02:09.284 --> 02:11.369
Somewhere he could go, and it'll
be safe during a siege,

02:11.494 --> 02:13.496
but still be close enough
to lead his nation.

02:13.622 --> 02:15.248
If it's
an underground secret bunker

02:15.373 --> 02:18.376
we're looking for,
I'm just the girl to find it.

02:18.460 --> 02:20.253
The Mechanist gave me
this timing device.

02:20.378 --> 02:21.671
It looks like we've got about
ten minutes

02:21.796 --> 02:22.964
until the full eclipse.

02:23.089 --> 02:24.841
Ten minutes to find
the Fire Lord.

02:24.966 --> 02:26.343
We can still do this.

02:26.468 --> 02:28.053
We can still win the day.

02:28.136 --> 02:29.137
Wait.

02:29.220 --> 02:31.681
If they knew we were coming,
it could all be a trap.

02:31.765 --> 02:33.808
Maybe we should use the time
we have left to make sure

02:33.892 --> 02:35.936
we all get out of here safely.

02:36.061 --> 02:37.812
Everyone who's here today
came prepared

02:37.938 --> 02:40.231
to risk everything
for this mission.

02:40.357 --> 02:42.108
They know what's at stake.

02:42.233 --> 02:45.111
If there's still a chance
and there's still hope,

02:45.236 --> 02:47.280
I think they would
want Aang to go for it.

02:47.405 --> 02:48.573
What do you think?

02:48.698 --> 02:50.075
You're the one
who has to face the Fire Lord.

02:50.492 --> 02:52.160
Whatever you decide,
I'm with you.

02:52.285 --> 02:55.538
♪

02:55.664 --> 02:58.458
I've got to try.

02:58.541 --> 03:00.794
[ roars ]

03:00.919 --> 03:03.838
♪

03:03.922 --> 03:05.548
Do you feel
anything down there?

03:05.882 --> 03:06.925
Yep.

03:07.050 --> 03:08.134
There are natural tunnels
crisscrossing

03:08.259 --> 03:09.928
through the inside
of the volcano.

03:10.053 --> 03:11.054
Anything else?

03:11.179 --> 03:12.555
Is there a structure somewhere?

03:15.183 --> 03:17.686
There's something big, dense,
and made of metal

03:17.811 --> 03:19.562
deep in the heart
of the volcano.

03:19.688 --> 03:21.398
Sounds like
a secret bunker to me.

03:22.607 --> 03:23.942
[ crash ]

03:25.485 --> 03:26.695
Stay safe.

03:26.820 --> 03:28.279
We'll be back soon.

03:30.782 --> 03:32.117
This way!
That one's a dead end.

03:32.242 --> 03:33.910
SOKKA: What would we do without you?

03:34.035 --> 03:35.829
Perish and burn in hot magma.

03:35.954 --> 03:37.205
Yeah, pretty much.

03:40.917 --> 03:42.627
TOPH: The tunnel continues
on the other side

03:42.752 --> 03:44.337
and it leads
right to the bunker.

03:44.462 --> 03:46.256
We'll have to be
fast but careful.

03:46.381 --> 03:47.841
Ah!

03:47.966 --> 03:49.300
How was that careful?

03:49.426 --> 03:50.510
I was wrong.

03:50.635 --> 03:52.762
We need to be fast,
careful, and lucky.

03:52.887 --> 03:55.015
♪

03:55.140 --> 03:59.602
[ lava hissing ]

03:59.728 --> 04:00.895
SOKKA: There's no floor!

04:01.021 --> 04:03.481
It's just a river of lava.

04:03.565 --> 04:05.942
AANG: Climb aboard
and hold on tight.

04:06.026 --> 04:08.069
[ screaming ]

04:08.153 --> 04:12.657
♪

04:20.081 --> 04:21.708
SOKKA: That's some door!

04:21.833 --> 04:25.211
♪

04:25.295 --> 04:26.504
[ metal banging ]

04:26.629 --> 04:27.964
Not a problem.

04:28.089 --> 04:29.257
♪

04:29.382 --> 04:31.009
[ metal banging ]

04:31.134 --> 04:33.678
♪

04:33.803 --> 04:36.306
[ metal banging ]

04:37.891 --> 04:40.852
I am so glad we
added you to the group.

04:40.935 --> 04:44.939
♪

04:47.567 --> 04:51.821
[ missiles exploding ]

04:54.324 --> 04:59.204
[ crash ]

04:59.370 --> 05:03.875
♪

05:03.958 --> 05:05.043
Retreat!

05:05.126 --> 05:07.128
Everyone move to the secondary
defensive position!

05:07.212 --> 05:08.379
Retreat!

05:08.588 --> 05:11.049
♪

05:11.758 --> 05:13.927
The eclipse
is only minutes away.

05:14.010 --> 05:17.097
We should be able to make it up
the hill by the time it starts

05:17.180 --> 05:20.391
and secure the entire palace
by the time it's finished!

05:20.475 --> 05:23.978
MEN: [ screaming ]

05:24.229 --> 05:25.897
We can wait here if you want.

05:25.980 --> 05:28.691
No. I want to press forward
with the others.

05:32.779 --> 05:35.615
[ whistling ]

05:35.740 --> 05:37.367
[ gasps ]

05:37.492 --> 05:40.036
♪

05:40.120 --> 05:42.122
The Fire Lord's chamber
is that way down the hall

05:42.205 --> 05:45.083
to the left and up the stairs.
You can't miss it.

05:45.208 --> 05:46.626
Thanks.

05:50.505 --> 05:52.841
[ sighs ]

05:52.966 --> 05:54.384
[ whistles ]

05:54.509 --> 05:57.137
♪

05:57.220 --> 05:59.305
Only 30 seconds
until the total eclipse.

05:59.430 --> 06:03.268
♪

06:03.393 --> 06:05.270
[ deep breathing ]

06:05.770 --> 06:07.063
I'm ready.

06:07.147 --> 06:09.983
I'm ready to face the Fire Lord.

06:10.066 --> 06:13.153
[ door opens ]

06:13.236 --> 06:15.572
So, you are alive after all.

06:15.655 --> 06:17.824
♪

06:17.907 --> 06:19.826
I had a hunch
that you survived.

06:19.909 --> 06:20.994
But it doesn't matter,

06:21.119 --> 06:23.121
I've known about the invasion
for months.

06:23.288 --> 06:27.333
♪

06:28.877 --> 06:30.336
I'm ready to face you.

06:30.587 --> 06:35.008
♪

06:35.175 --> 06:38.052
Prince Zuko,
what are you doing here?

06:38.469 --> 06:40.597
♪

06:43.558 --> 06:47.854
♪

06:53.234 --> 06:55.320
The eclipse is starting!

06:55.445 --> 06:57.113
Put on your eclipse glasses.

06:57.238 --> 07:02.285
♪

07:10.126 --> 07:12.337
Why are you here?

07:12.462 --> 07:14.130
I'm here to tell the truth.

07:14.255 --> 07:17.800
Telling the truth
during the middle of an eclipse.

07:17.926 --> 07:19.844
This should be interesting.

07:25.391 --> 07:27.268
First of all, in Ba Sing Se,

07:27.393 --> 07:30.647
it was Azula who took down
the Avatar, not me.

07:30.772 --> 07:32.899
Why would she
lie to me about that?

07:33.024 --> 07:34.776
Because the Avatar
is not dead.

07:34.901 --> 07:36.152
He survived.

07:36.277 --> 07:37.528
What?

07:37.654 --> 07:39.739
In fact, he's probably
is leading this invasion.

07:39.864 --> 07:41.449
He could be on us right now.

07:41.574 --> 07:42.867
Get out!

07:42.951 --> 07:45.578
Get out of my sight right now
if you know what's good for you.

07:45.703 --> 07:46.746
That's another thing.

07:46.871 --> 07:49.040
I'm not taking orders
from you anymore.

07:49.165 --> 07:51.167
You will obey me

07:51.292 --> 07:54.337
or this defiant breath
will be your last!

07:56.339 --> 07:57.840
Think again!

07:57.966 --> 08:00.843
I am going to speak my mind,
and you are going to listen!

08:00.969 --> 08:03.388
♪

08:03.513 --> 08:04.597
Where is he?

08:04.722 --> 08:06.766
Where is the Fire Lord?

08:06.891 --> 08:08.977
Hm, you mean I'm not
good enough for you?

08:09.102 --> 08:11.312
You're hurting my feelings.

08:11.437 --> 08:14.190
Stop wasting our time
and give us the information.

08:14.315 --> 08:17.110
You're powerless right now, so
you're in no position to refuse.

08:17.235 --> 08:18.778
And stick to the truth.

08:18.903 --> 08:21.072
I'll be able to tell
if you're lying.

08:21.197 --> 08:22.282
Are you sure?

08:22.407 --> 08:24.701
I'm a pretty good liar.

08:24.826 --> 08:27.578
I am a 400-foot-tall
purple platypus bear

08:27.704 --> 08:31.249
with pink horns
and silver wings.

08:31.374 --> 08:32.792
Okay, you're good, I admit it.

08:35.920 --> 08:38.548
But you really ought to consider
telling the truth anyway.

08:38.673 --> 08:41.259
♪

08:41.384 --> 08:44.095
[ crash ]

08:46.389 --> 08:49.517
When I left Ba Sing Se,
I brought home some souvenirs.

08:49.684 --> 08:51.561
♪

08:51.686 --> 08:53.229
Dai Li agents.

08:53.354 --> 08:57.734
♪

09:07.243 --> 09:09.037
Surround the periphery!

09:09.287 --> 09:12.540
We have to secure the palace
by the time the eclipse is over.

09:12.665 --> 09:15.752
Otherwise, we'll be in
for the fight of our lives.

09:20.548 --> 09:21.799
TYRO: Stop!

09:21.924 --> 09:24.135
Surrender peacefully,
and we won't harm you.

09:24.469 --> 09:25.928
We'll never surrender.

09:26.054 --> 09:30.058
♪

09:31.225 --> 09:32.769
Er, okay, we surrender.

09:32.894 --> 09:34.979
♪

09:35.104 --> 09:36.147
HAKODA: There it is.

09:36.272 --> 09:38.232
The Fire Nation royal palace.

09:38.358 --> 09:39.984
We've come so far.

09:40.109 --> 09:41.569
It's not over yet.

09:41.694 --> 09:44.530
♪

09:44.655 --> 09:46.199
For so long, all I wanted

09:46.324 --> 09:48.826
was for you to love me,
to accept me.

09:48.951 --> 09:50.745
I thought it was my honor
that I wanted.

09:50.870 --> 09:54.165
But really, I was just
trying to please you.

09:54.290 --> 09:58.920
You, my father, who banished me
just for talking out of turn.

09:59.045 --> 10:02.131
My father, who challenged me―
a 13-year-old boy―

10:02.256 --> 10:03.674
to an Agni Kai.

10:03.800 --> 10:06.677
How can you possibly
justify a duel with a child?

10:06.803 --> 10:08.554
It was to teach you respect.

10:08.679 --> 10:09.722
It was cruel!

10:09.847 --> 10:10.932
And it was wrong!

10:11.057 --> 10:12.600
Then you've learned nothing.

10:12.725 --> 10:15.353
No, I've learnt everything!

10:15.478 --> 10:17.647
And I had to learn it on my own.

10:17.772 --> 10:19.774
Growing up, we were taught
that the Fire Nation

10:19.899 --> 10:22.276
was the greatest civilization
in history.

10:22.402 --> 10:25.071
And somehow, the war was our way
of sharing our greatness

10:25.196 --> 10:27.240
with the rest of the world.

10:27.365 --> 10:29.742
What an amazing lie that was.

10:29.867 --> 10:32.870
The people of the world are
terrified by the Fire Nation!

10:32.995 --> 10:35.623
They don't see our greatness,
they hate us!

10:35.748 --> 10:36.999
And we deserve it.

10:37.125 --> 10:39.669
We've created an era
of fear in the world.

10:39.794 --> 10:42.672
And if we don't want the world
to destroy itself,

10:42.797 --> 10:47.343
we need to replace it with
an era of peace and kindness.

10:47.468 --> 10:49.595
[ laughing ]

10:49.720 --> 10:52.348
Your Uncle has gotten to you,
hasn't he?

10:53.975 --> 10:56.436
Yes. He has.

10:59.522 --> 11:01.858
[ crash ]

11:01.983 --> 11:05.278
♪

11:07.780 --> 11:10.158
[ rock crumbling ]

11:10.283 --> 11:14.620
♪

11:35.099 --> 11:36.392
[ crash ]

11:36.517 --> 11:38.478
[ grunts ]

11:38.603 --> 11:42.398
[ rocks crashing ]

11:42.523 --> 11:48.488
♪

12:00.333 --> 12:06.047
♪

12:20.144 --> 12:21.270
I can't pin her down.

12:21.395 --> 12:22.772
She's too quick.

12:22.897 --> 12:27.235
♪

12:31.948 --> 12:34.867
[ grunting ]

12:37.495 --> 12:40.498
Wait! Aang, Toph,
stop attacking.

12:40.623 --> 12:41.749
Don't you see what she's doing?

12:41.874 --> 12:43.292
She's just playing with us.

12:43.417 --> 12:45.336
She's not even trying
to win this fight!

12:45.461 --> 12:48.172
Not true, I'm
giving it my all.

12:48.297 --> 12:50.758
You're trying to keep us here
and waste all our time!

12:50.883 --> 12:52.009
Um, right.

12:52.134 --> 12:54.053
I think your friend
just said that, genius.

12:54.178 --> 12:55.388
And since you can't see,

12:55.513 --> 12:58.349
I should tell you
I'm rolling my eyes.

12:58.474 --> 13:00.101
I'll roll your whole head!

13:00.226 --> 13:01.852
She's just baiting you again.

13:01.978 --> 13:03.521
Okay, so what do we do?

13:03.646 --> 13:05.022
Just ignore her?

13:05.147 --> 13:07.608
We don't have a choice,
we just have to get out of here

13:07.733 --> 13:10.528
and find the Fire Lord
on our own somehow.

13:10.611 --> 13:11.654
It's a trap.

13:11.779 --> 13:13.406
Don't say I didn't warn you.

13:13.531 --> 13:15.408
Ignore!

13:15.533 --> 13:17.994
So, Sokka's your name, right?

13:18.119 --> 13:21.706
My favorite prisoner used
to mention you all the time.

13:21.831 --> 13:24.208
She was convinced that you were
going to come rescue her.

13:24.333 --> 13:28.337
Of course, you never came,
and she gave up on you.

13:28.462 --> 13:31.549
[ grunting ]

13:31.674 --> 13:33.092
Come and get it.

13:33.217 --> 13:36.679
♪

13:36.804 --> 13:39.390
[ grunts ]

13:39.515 --> 13:42.518
Where is Suki?

13:44.145 --> 13:46.480
ZUKO: After I leave here today,
I'm going to free Uncle Iroh

13:46.606 --> 13:47.690
from his prison.

13:47.815 --> 13:49.817
And I'm going to beg
for his forgiveness.

13:49.942 --> 13:52.069
He is the one who has been
a real father to me.

13:52.194 --> 13:54.697
[ chuckles ]
That's just beautiful.

13:54.822 --> 13:58.284
Maybe he can pass down to you
the ways of tea and failure.

13:58.409 --> 14:00.494
But I've come to an even more
important decision.

14:02.121 --> 14:03.956
I'm going to join the Avatar.

14:04.081 --> 14:05.791
And I'm going to help him
defeat you.

14:05.916 --> 14:07.293
Really?

14:07.418 --> 14:09.629
Since you're
a full-blown traitor now,

14:09.754 --> 14:11.881
and you want me gone, why wait?

14:12.006 --> 14:15.009
I'm powerless,
you've got your swords,

14:15.134 --> 14:17.094
why don't you just do it now?

14:17.219 --> 14:19.180
Because I know
my own destiny.

14:19.305 --> 14:22.016
Taking you down
is the Avatar's destiny.

14:22.141 --> 14:23.726
[ metal clangs ]

14:23.851 --> 14:25.561
Goodbye.

14:25.686 --> 14:27.730
Coward! You think
you're brave enough to face me,

14:27.855 --> 14:29.982
but you'll only do it
during the eclipse.

14:30.107 --> 14:31.776
If you have any real courage,

14:31.901 --> 14:34.695
you'll stick around
until the Sun comes out.

14:34.820 --> 14:38.032
Don't you want to know
what happened to your mother?

14:38.157 --> 14:40.910
♪

14:51.295 --> 14:53.005
ZUKO: What happened that night?

14:53.130 --> 14:56.592
My father―Fire Lord Azulon―
had commanded me

14:56.717 --> 15:01.013
to do the unthinkable to you,
my own son.

15:01.138 --> 15:03.057
And I was going to do it.

15:03.182 --> 15:04.475
Your Mother found out

15:04.600 --> 15:07.645
and swore she would
protect you at any cost.

15:07.770 --> 15:11.190
She knew I wanted the throne,
and she proposed a plan.

15:11.315 --> 15:14.610
A plan in which I would become
Fire Lord

15:14.735 --> 15:18.114
and your life would be spared.

15:18.239 --> 15:20.366
Where's Suki?

15:20.491 --> 15:21.867
Answer me!

15:21.992 --> 15:25.287
Sokka, she won't talk.

15:25.413 --> 15:27.081
Where are you keeping her?

15:28.165 --> 15:31.627
Your Mother did vicious,
treasonous things that night.

15:32.128 --> 15:34.797
She knew the consequences
and accepted them.

15:34.922 --> 15:38.509
For her treason,
she was banished.

15:38.634 --> 15:40.010
So she's alive.

15:40.136 --> 15:42.221
Perhaps.

15:42.346 --> 15:46.225
Now I realize that banishment
is far too merciful a penalty

15:46.350 --> 15:47.935
for treason.

15:48.060 --> 15:51.397
Your penalty
will be far steeper.

15:51.522 --> 15:54.316
♪

15:54.442 --> 16:00.239
[ lightning zapping ]

16:01.490 --> 16:04.034
-[ explosion ]
-[ grunts ]

16:04.326 --> 16:09.415
♪

16:12.585 --> 16:14.879
Oh. Sounds like
the fire-bending's back on.

16:15.004 --> 16:18.090
[ grunting ]

16:18.215 --> 16:21.802
♪

16:24.555 --> 16:26.182
Dad's all the way
at the end of the hall

16:26.265 --> 16:28.100
and down the secret stairway
on the left.

16:28.225 --> 16:31.270
I'm sure he'll be more
than happy to see you now.

16:31.395 --> 16:32.605
SOKKA: I fell for it!

16:32.730 --> 16:34.482
I used up all our time.

16:34.607 --> 16:36.358
It's not your fault, Sokka.

16:36.484 --> 16:37.985
Azula was ready for us.

16:38.110 --> 16:40.613
She had every move planned out.

16:40.738 --> 16:42.323
And now it's too late.

16:42.448 --> 16:44.450
AANG: Maybe it's not too late.

16:44.575 --> 16:47.828
The eclipse is over, but I can
face the Fire Lord anyway.

16:47.953 --> 16:48.954
No.

16:49.038 --> 16:50.164
I don't think
that's a good idea.

16:50.289 --> 16:51.624
But I'm ready!

16:51.707 --> 16:55.085
I came here with a job to do,
and everyone's counting on me.

16:55.211 --> 16:57.296
The Fire Lord knew
we were coming this time.

16:57.421 --> 16:59.882
We thought we had surprise
on our side, but we didn't.

17:00.007 --> 17:01.425
It just wasn't our day.

17:01.550 --> 17:04.512
What we need to do now
is go help our friends.

17:04.637 --> 17:06.055
I guess you guys are right.

17:06.180 --> 17:07.515
SOKKA: You'll have another chance.

17:07.640 --> 17:09.099
I know you will.

17:14.146 --> 17:15.397
BATO: What should we do, Hakoda?

17:15.523 --> 17:17.191
Shouldn't something
have happened by now?

17:17.316 --> 17:18.442
I don't know.

17:18.567 --> 17:20.152
But now that the eclipse
is over,

17:20.277 --> 17:23.656
I expect we're going to see
some Firebenders any minute.

17:23.906 --> 17:28.035
♪

17:32.289 --> 17:34.208
MECHANIST: My own invention.

17:34.542 --> 17:36.085
Oh, this is terrible!

17:36.210 --> 17:42.132
♪

17:48.097 --> 17:49.348
They're back!

17:49.473 --> 17:55.396
♪

18:03.320 --> 18:04.780
It was all a trap.

18:04.905 --> 18:07.658
Azula knew we were coming, and
she's plotted out every move.

18:08.534 --> 18:10.786
We just got to get to the beach
as fast as we can.

18:10.995 --> 18:12.079
If we can make it
to the submarines,

18:12.162 --> 18:13.539
maybe we can get away safely.

18:13.664 --> 18:16.125
They've got air power,
but so do I!

18:16.250 --> 18:18.168
♪

18:18.294 --> 18:20.254
I'm going to do what I can
to slow them down.

18:23.299 --> 18:25.175
Appa, you and I can help, too.

18:25.301 --> 18:28.178
♪

18:28.304 --> 18:30.472
Everyone, let's get back
to the subs!

18:30.598 --> 18:35.394
♪

18:48.908 --> 18:51.535
[ gunfire exploding ]

18:51.660 --> 18:56.248
[ growling ]

18:56.373 --> 19:00.002
♪

19:00.127 --> 19:01.462
KATARA: We can't keep them all back.

19:01.587 --> 19:03.464
They're too many of them!

19:03.589 --> 19:04.924
Let's join the others.

19:05.049 --> 19:09.929
♪

19:17.436 --> 19:18.437
Uncle!

19:18.562 --> 19:23.525
♪

19:23.651 --> 19:24.902
Where is my Uncle?

19:25.027 --> 19:26.320
He's gone.

19:26.445 --> 19:28.280
He busted himself out.

19:28.405 --> 19:30.115
I―I've never seen
anything like it!

19:30.240 --> 19:32.701
He was like a one man army!

19:32.826 --> 19:38.207
♪

19:40.125 --> 19:41.293
Try and find cover!

19:41.418 --> 19:42.962
I think we're about
to see some bombs.

19:43.087 --> 19:47.758
♪

19:49.426 --> 19:54.723
[ bombs exploding ]

19:54.848 --> 19:56.684
♪

19:56.809 --> 20:00.854
MEN: [ screaming ]

20:02.773 --> 20:05.567
KATARA: Why aren't they turning around
to attack us again?

20:06.151 --> 20:08.445
They're headed for the beach.

20:08.570 --> 20:10.239
They're going to destroy
the submarines!

20:10.364 --> 20:11.865
How are we all
going to escape?

20:11.991 --> 20:13.701
We're not.

20:14.159 --> 20:16.453
Then our only choice
is to stand and fight.

20:16.578 --> 20:19.331
We have the Avatar,
we could still win!

20:19.456 --> 20:23.335
Yes, with the Avatar we could
still win on another day.

20:23.460 --> 20:24.920
You kids have to leave.

20:25.045 --> 20:27.047
You have to escape
on Appa together.

20:27.172 --> 20:28.173
What?

20:28.298 --> 20:29.883
We can't leave you behind.

20:30.009 --> 20:32.136
We won't leave anyone behind.

20:32.261 --> 20:34.388
You're our only chance
in the long run.

20:34.513 --> 20:37.099
You and Sokka have to go
with Aang somewhere safe.

20:37.224 --> 20:39.518
It's the only way
to keep hope alive.

20:39.643 --> 20:42.021
The youngest of our group
should go with you.

20:42.146 --> 20:44.773
The adults will stay behind
and surrender.

20:44.898 --> 20:48.861
We'll be prisoners, but we'll
all survive this battle.

20:48.986 --> 20:52.114
I've got some experience
with the Fire Nation prisons.

20:52.239 --> 20:54.908
It's not going to be easy,
but we'll get by.

20:55.034 --> 20:56.201
They're at the beach already!

20:56.535 --> 21:01.123
♪

21:06.712 --> 21:10.674
[ bombs exploding ]

21:20.184 --> 21:24.021
[ explosions continue ]

21:24.271 --> 21:29.735
♪

21:36.867 --> 21:38.077
Bye, son.

21:38.202 --> 21:39.495
Bye, Dad.

21:39.620 --> 21:41.371
I'm really proud of you.

21:41.497 --> 21:44.666
♪

21:44.792 --> 21:47.127
[ grunts ]
I'll miss you, Pipsqueak.

21:47.252 --> 21:48.796
Take care, The Duke.

21:50.923 --> 21:52.341
We'll be back for you, Dad.

21:52.466 --> 21:54.510
If we don't escape
on our own first.

21:54.635 --> 21:57.805
♪

21:57.930 --> 22:01.266
We lost today,
but we've never been this close.

22:01.391 --> 22:04.728
We tasted victory,
and that counts for something.

22:04.853 --> 22:06.730
We'll miss you, Dad.

22:08.065 --> 22:09.108
SOKKA: Bye, Dad.

22:09.358 --> 22:11.151
We won't be apart
for too long this time.

22:11.276 --> 22:12.861
I promise.

22:12.986 --> 22:18.909
♪

22:23.372 --> 22:27.084
Thank you all for being
so brave and so strong.

22:27.209 --> 22:28.710
I'm going to make this
up to you.

22:31.296 --> 22:36.301
[ growling ]

22:36.426 --> 22:41.098
♪

22:45.811 --> 22:47.229
Should we follow them,
Princess?

22:47.354 --> 22:49.314
AZULA: No. They're too fast.

22:49.439 --> 22:51.608
It doesn't matter,
they'll be back.

22:51.733 --> 22:54.945
♪

22:55.070 --> 22:56.613
I know just the place
for us to go

22:56.697 --> 22:58.073
where we'll be safe for a while.

22:58.198 --> 22:59.658
The Western Air Temple.

22:59.783 --> 23:01.076
[ grunting ]

23:04.121 --> 23:09.585
♪

23:20.053 --> 23:24.558
MALE:
[ vocalizing drumbeats ]

23:30.480 --> 23:37.196
♪

23:53.545 --> 24:00.052
♪
